WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.197 --> 00:00:04.733
This is Voice plus Vision Incident Reporter, a local proof of concept.

2
00:00:04.733 --> 00:00:09.464
A spoken report and a photo go in; a structured incident draft comes out,

3
00:00:09.464 --> 00:00:13.093
and nothing becomes a record until a person approves it.

4
00:00:14.103 --> 00:00:18.551
A field reporter signs in. Every account and every action is logged.

5
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:23.519
The reporter uploads a short voice report and a photo of the scene.

6
00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:28.540
The server checks the file type, size, duration and whether the files decode,

7
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.149
and strips location data from the image.

8
00:00:31.744 --> 00:00:36.495
Everything runs on this laptop's CPU: Whisper transcribes the audio,

9
00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:38.452
and CLIP analyses the image.

10
00:00:38.759 --> 00:00:40.926
Here is the report being played back.

11
00:00:40.876 --> 00:00:44.864
[Report, synthetic voice] The river flooded our street about twenty minutes ago and the water

12
00:00:44.864 --> 00:00:45.817
is still rising.

13
00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:47.067
Three cars are stuck,

14
00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:50.817
and an older couple is stranded in the house at 14 Mill Street.

15
00:00:49.509 --> 00:00:52.802
The transcript is shown with the incident terms it found.

16
00:00:52.802 --> 00:00:56.732
If the recogniser misheard something, the reporter corrects it here,

17
00:00:56.732 --> 00:00:59.332
and the original is kept for the audit trail.

18
00:00:59.947 --> 00:01:04.139
The report is classified three ways: text only, image only,

19
00:01:04.139 --> 00:01:06.129
and text and image combined.

20
00:01:06.728 --> 00:01:11.828
Then the two sources are compared. They agree on flood water. The street address,

21
00:01:11.828 --> 00:01:16.866
the time and the stranded couple come only from the report. A weak image signal,

22
00:01:16.866 --> 00:01:21.147
possible power lines, is marked as uncertain and becomes a question.

23
00:01:21.775 --> 00:01:24.582
The draft proposes a category and a summary.

24
00:01:24.582 --> 00:01:28.857
Every claim links back to the words or image evidence it came from.

25
00:01:29.478 --> 00:01:31.886
When the sources contradict each other,

26
00:01:31.886 --> 00:01:34.851
like a report of a fire with a photo of a flood,

27
00:01:34.851 --> 00:01:38.927
the system lists both sides and does not decide which one is true.

28
00:01:39.541 --> 00:01:43.473
A reviewer, who is not the reporter, answers the open question,

29
00:01:43.473 --> 00:01:45.720
confirms the evidence, and approves.

30
00:01:47.353 --> 00:01:51.630
Only now is there an approved record, with a hash, the reviewer's name,

31
00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.678
and every change in the audit log.

32
00:01:54.353 --> 00:01:58.196
Measured on 955 held-out CrisisMMD posts,

33
00:01:58.196 --> 00:02:02.508
combining text and image scored 0.82 macro F1,

34
00:02:02.508 --> 00:02:08.132
versus 0.79 for the image alone and 0.74 for the text alone.

35
00:02:08.132 --> 00:02:13.850
The gain over the image alone was not statistically reliable.

36
00:02:15.103 --> 00:02:20.004
One honest limit: there is no real dataset of spoken incident reports,

37
00:02:20.004 --> 00:02:24.625
so speech was tested on synthetic voices and audiobook recordings,

38
00:02:24.625 --> 00:02:26.025
not on real callers.

39
00:02:27.119 --> 00:02:29.967
Voice plus Vision Incident Reporter. Code,

40
00:02:29.967 --> 00:02:32.816
results and credits are in the repository.
